<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tomé de Sousa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1549</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tomé de Sousa was a Portuguese nobleman who became the first Governor-General of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> in 1549. His appointment partly replaced the decentralised hereditary captaincy system, which had produced very uneven results. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> profile notes that he established <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> as the colonial capital and began building a more systematic administration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tome-de-sousa.jpg" alt="Tomé de Sousa" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Samory Pereira Santos from Salvador, Brazil · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thom%C3%A9_de_Souza_(3712120735).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
